主线有 29 个内核模块引用 tl.extra.cuda。Triton 算 kernel 的 cache_key 时会遍历
语法树并逐个解析全局属性链，连死 constexpr 分支里的也解析，而 triton-ascend 只
提供 tl.extra.cann。结果是在哈希阶段就抛 AttributeError，内核体一行没跑——表现
为服务在捕获解码图时崩溃。

本提交发布一个空的 tl.extra.cuda 子模块，两个 PDL 原语是空的 @triton.jit 函数：
只需满足语法树遍历，永远不会被调用。PDL 是纯调度优化，不涉及数值。在真有
tl.extra.cuda 的 CUDA 环境上 install() 直接返回，模块失效。
---
 .../srt/hardware_backend/npu/__init__.py      |  7 +++
 .../hardware_backend/npu/triton_pdl_compat.py | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 68 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/__init__.py
 create mode 100644 python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/triton_pdl_compat.py

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/__init__.py b/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/__init__.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1836ad9575
--- /dev/null
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/__init__.py
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+"""Ascend NPU hardware backend.
+
+Importing any NPU backend module installs the triton-ascend PDL compatibility
+shim first -- see ``triton_pdl_compat`` for why it is needed and why it is safe.
+"""
+
+from sglang.srt.hardware_backend.npu import triton_pdl_compat  # noqa: F401
diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/triton_pdl_compat.py b/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/triton_pdl_compat.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..3b6a4c81b6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/npu/triton_pdl_compat.py
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+"""Make ``tl.extra.cuda`` resolvable under triton-ascend.
+
+Mainline sglang guards every PDL (programmatic dependent launch) call behind a
+``USE_GDC: tl.constexpr`` that ``is_arch_support_pdl()`` leaves False on Ascend,
+so the calls never execute.  That is not enough.  Triton computes a kernel's
+cache key by walking its AST and *resolving* every global attribute chain it
+finds -- including chains inside dead ``tl.constexpr`` branches
+(``triton/runtime/jit.py``, ``JITFunction.cache_key`` -> ``visit_Attribute`` ->
+``getattr``).  triton-ascend ships ``triton.language.extra.cann`` and no
+``.cuda``, so that walk raises
+
+    AttributeError: module 'triton.language.extra' has no attribute 'cuda'
+
+before a single line of the kernel body runs.  Observed as a scheduler crash
+during decode graph capture, via
+``kernels/ops/attention/fla/fused_sigmoid_gating_recurrent.py``.
+
+29 kernel modules in mainline reference ``tl.extra.cuda``; patching each one
+would be a large diff that conflicts with every upstream touch of those files.
+Publish a ``cuda`` submodule instead, whose two PDL primitives are empty
+``@triton.jit`` functions.  They satisfy the AST walk and can never run: the
+only call sites sit under ``if USE_GDC:`` with USE_GDC False on this platform.
+PDL is a scheduling optimisation, so nothing numerical depends on it.
+
+Not installed when a real ``tl.extra.cuda`` is present -- on CUDA this module
+is inert.
+"""
+
+import sys
+import types
+
+import triton
+import triton.language as tl
+
+_MODULE_NAME = "triton.language.extra.cuda"
+
+
+def install() -> bool:
+    """Publish a no-op ``tl.extra.cuda``. Returns True if it installed one."""
+    extra = getattr(tl, "extra", None)
+    if extra is None or hasattr(extra, "cuda"):
+        return False
+
+    module = types.ModuleType(_MODULE_NAME)
+
+    @triton.jit
+    def gdc_wait():
+        pass
+
+    @triton.jit
+    def gdc_launch_dependents():
+        pass
+
+    module.gdc_wait = gdc_wait
+    module.gdc_launch_dependents = gdc_launch_dependents
+    extra.cuda = module
+    sys.modules[_MODULE_NAME] = module
+    return True
+
+
+install()
